<title>INDIA: India Essar 1996/97 1st half shows loss.</title>
<headline>India Essar 1996/97 1st half shows loss.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	(476.1)  vs     697.2</p>
<p>    Sales	    9,370.6   vs    2,963.7</p>
<p>    Other income     272.0   vs	 59.6</p>
<p>    Expenditure    7,184.9   vs    2,103.7</p>
<p>    Gross profit   2,457.7   vs	919.6</p>
<p>    Interest costs 1,717.1   vs	 00.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation   1,216.7   vs	221.8</p>
<p>    Tax		  Nil     vs	 Nil</p>
<p>Note: Figure in brackets represent loss. Private steel maker Essar Steel Ltd said sales for the six months exclude inter-divisional transfer of hot-briquetted iron valued at 1.79 billion rupees and sales of hot-rolled coil plant's trial production of 1.51 billion rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
